ReadyStack 0002: RPM bumps in KubeVirt's own lock (x86_64, CentOS Stream 9 trees only).

Each bump replaces one WORKSPACE rpm() rule (name, sha256, URL) and every rpmtree label naming it in rpm/BUILD.bazel,
the way bazeldnf writes them. The libvirt-libs_x86_64_cs9 tar2files list then names libcrypto.so.3.5.9 and
libssl.so.3.5.9, exactly what KubeVirt's own `bazel run //rpm:ldd_x86_64_cs9` regenerates (verified). rpm --test on
every x86_64 cs9 tree resolves the same dependencies before and after. Bumps (from rpm-bumps.tsv):
  openssl-1__3.5.8-1.el9.x86_64 -> openssl-1__3.5.9-1.el9.x86_64  (CVE-2026-84782 high (RHEL 1:3.5.8-2.el9_8), CVE-2026-14456 high (RHEL 1:3.5.8-1.el9_8); CS9 rebased to 3.5.9)
  openssl-libs-1__3.5.8-1.el9.x86_64 -> openssl-libs-1__3.5.9-1.el9.x86_64  (same source as openssl)
  openssl-fips-provider-1__3.5.8-1.el9.x86_64 -> openssl-fips-provider-1__3.5.9-1.el9.x86_64  (same source as openssl)
  pcre2-0__10.40-6.el9.x86_64 -> pcre2-0__10.40-7.el9.x86_64  (CVE-2026-86145, CVE-2026-89161 high (changelog 10.40-7: Backport multiple CVE fixes))
  pcre2-syntax-0__10.40-6.el9.x86_64 -> pcre2-syntax-0__10.40-7.el9.x86_64  (same source as pcre2)
  ca-certificates-0__2026.2.90_v9.0.316-90.0.el9.x86_64 -> ca-certificates-0__2026.2.92_v9.0.319-91.3.el9.x86_64  (CVE-2026-114406 critical (RHEL 2026.2.92_v9.0.319-90.3.el9_8))
  libevent-0__2.1.12-8.el9.x86_64 -> libevent-0__2.1.13-1.el9.x86_64  (CVE-2026-63382/63383/63384/63385/63387/63388 high (changelog 2.1.13-1))
  libpcap-14__1.10.0-4.el9.x86_64 -> libpcap-14__1.10.0-5.el9.x86_64  (CVE-2026-0799 high (changelog 14:1.10.0-5))
  xz-0__5.2.5-8.el9.x86_64 -> xz-0__5.2.5-10.el9.x86_64  (Scout flags CVE-2022-1271 high on 5.2.5-8.el9 (el9 vs RHEL el9_0; 5.2.5-8 already resolves it); -10 sorts above)
  xz-libs-0__5.2.5-8.el9.x86_64 -> xz-libs-0__5.2.5-10.el9.x86_64  (same source as xz)

